  clock: 2  # 1e4f
  nonce: 1e4f  # 1e4f
  message: "Swift prerequisite landed: INV-kotob satisfied in PR #757 (dev 75f1373611) — the module slot carries the receiver's TYPE (declared / annotated / constructed / singleton-or-enum-case local / inline type head), never the variable; project types (generics stripped) ride in receiver_type_hint only; an instance never binds a static member by bare name. Measured: churn Alamofire 786 gains / 0 type losses / 9 Set<X>→Set re-keys / 5 resolved→typed (mis-bindings to test-only static extension members, un-bound), Vernissage 2236 gains / 0 losses / 1 re-key; io Alamofire 27→31 (6 real FileManager boundaries surfaced, 1 phantom Tier-2 URLSession.dataTask link gone), Vernissage 8→8 (3 lost in pass 1, all recovered). What this item still owes: (1) the RETURN-TYPE REGISTRY consumer for swift and objc (a local bound to a method-call result — `let data = try await session.data(...)`, `let fm = makeManager()` — is still untyped; the registry interface WI-lalot's loader feeds is unchanged); (2) the objc half — declared receiver types from `T *x` declarations and `(T *)x` parameters — is scripted and baselined in the same lab dir (apply_higob_objc.py, test_objc_receiver_type_in_module_slot.py, arm A: AFNetworking 7 chains / SDWebImage 5) and is the next PR; (3) fixtures per binding form and the L4 measurement once the corpus item supplies more repos."  # 1e4f
