  clock: 4  # 36e8
  nonce: '36e8'  # 36e8
  message: "Swift registry consumer shipped in PR #760 (dev ccaefb05fa): Pass 1 registers `<Owner>.<func> -> bare T` via the base FileAnalysis.method_return_types (aggregated by TreeSitterAnalyzer.analyze, first writer wins — the dict WI-lalot's loader feeds); Pass 2 types a local bound to a call result (receiver-typed, type-head, bare-through-enclosing-then-free; try/await unwrapped). Fixtures per binding form: in-repo instance / static / bare / optional / collection-refused / try-await / unknown, plus a hand-fed library row through the same dict. Measured: churn Alamofire 89 gains / 76 untyped→resolved / 105 leak-given types dropped (read back as wrong or unscoped); Vernissage 72 gains / 137 dropped (for-loop and guard-let-from-library bindings); io unchanged on both. Remaining for this item: the objc registry consumer (scripted: apply_higob_objc_registry.py + test_objc_return_type_registry.py), chained `obj.make().frob()` receivers in swift (the chain HEAD is what `_extract_call_target` reports today), and L4 on findings once the corpus item supplies more repos."  # 36e8
